@ek3os/dsh-balance README · Requirements：- DeepSeek Harness `>=0.1.2-rc.1 <0.3.0-0` (verified against `0.2.0-rc.2`)
- The `web` profile
- A configured `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`

@ek3os/dsh-balance README · Compatibility notes：- The `slots` service moved from the retired `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime` package (last release `0.1.1-rc.2`) to `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-renderer`, so the peer declarations and `dsh.client.inject` list now name the renderer. DSH 0.2 refuses to load any bundle whose `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*` peers cannot be satisfied, which is what produced the `skipping profile bundle … is incompatible with dsh 0.2.0-rc.2` error.
- `dsh.client.inject` is the arrival-order contract: every listed package is loaded before this plugin's bundle, so `slots` is always available when `apply()` runs.
- The sidebar footer markup, stylesheet hooks, and layout class names are unchanged between 0.1.7-rc.2 and 0.2.0-rc.2, so the rendered result is identical.

